      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is not a copy so this method mutates the argument; which could be dangerous if the caller kept using rawAddr after calling this method.\nFortunately, currently this is not done because InetAddress#getAddress() returns a buffer that is not used by InetAddress, and IpPrefix#getRawAddress() returns a copy of its own buffer.\n\nOne way to avoid doing too many byte array copies would be to take an Inet4Address as argument directly instead of a byte[]. I think this can be in a followup.",
